WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.953
Install Nix packages

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:03.003
without ever running

00:00:02.815 --> 00:00:03.439
Nix

00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:05.227
nixpkgs holds over

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:06.076
one hundred forty

00:00:05.888 --> 00:00:06.996
thousand packages

00:00:07.091 --> 00:00:08.293
most already built

00:00:08.176 --> 00:00:09.048
and signed on

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.168
cache dot nixos

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.734
dot org

00:00:10.874 --> 00:00:12.465
Installing one normally

00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:13.633
means running Nix's

00:00:13.444 --> 00:00:14.411
evaluator

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.082
The nami package

00:00:15.893 --> 00:00:17.662
manager evaluates each

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:18.853
nixpkgs release once

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:19.678
ahead of time

00:00:19.879 --> 00:00:20.834
into one signed

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:21.801
catalog of store

00:00:21.613 --> 00:00:22.296
paths

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:23.770
versions and build

00:00:23.582 --> 00:00:24.513
definitions

00:00:25.046 --> 00:00:26.142
On your machine

00:00:26.308 --> 00:00:27.439
an install becomes

00:00:27.251 --> 00:00:28.135
a quick lookup

00:00:27.947 --> 00:00:29.185
plus a verified

00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:29.692
download

00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:30.906
and the catalog

00:00:30.718 --> 00:00:31.720
carries a hash

00:00:31.544 --> 00:00:32.593
of every build

00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:33.194
definition

00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:34.468
so one signature

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:35.187
vouches for them

00:00:35.046 --> 00:00:35.564
all

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.116
Full story on

00:00:36.927 --> 00:00:37.823
the dashboard
